Register the goodix_milanl driver in libfprint's build.

Two one-line additions to the upstream build so the in-tree driver is
compiled and its GType is registered. Apply with `patch -p1` from the
root of a libfprint 1.94.100 source tree,
then drop drivers/goodix_milanl.c and drivers/goodix_milanl_proto.h into place.

The driver is added to the DEFAULT set (no optional/virtual meson flag)
so an ordinary build ships it; it is FP_DEVICE_TYPE_VIRTUAL only at the
libfprint API level (it is reached over a socket, not USB/SPI).

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@ drivers_info = {
     'focaltech_moc': {},
     'mafpmoc': {},
     'secugen': {},
+    'goodix_milanl': {},

     # SPI driver (non-optional if SPI is available)
     'elanspi': { 'spi': true, 'helper': ['udev'], 'optional': not have_spi },
--- a/libfprint/meson.build
+++ b/libfprint/meson.build
@@ -139,6 +139,7 @@ driver_sources = {
     'focaltech_moc' : files('drivers/focaltech_moc/focaltech_moc.c'),
     'mafpmoc' : files('drivers/mafpmoc/mafpmoc.c'),
     'secugen' : files('drivers/secugen.c'),
+    'goodix_milanl' : files('drivers/goodix_milanl.c'),
 }

 helper_sources = {
